kspalaiologos/bzip3, release 1.5.3, plus two fixes.
Upstream: https://github.com/kspalaiologos/bzip3

libbz3.h, common.h and libsais.h are byte-identical to 1.5.3.
libbz3.c is 1.5.3 with two changes, both inside bz3_compress and
bz3_decompress, the only bzip3 entry points karyozip calls. Applying
these two to a fresh 1.5.3 reproduces this file byte for byte; that was
checked, not assumed.

1. bz3_compress, the size of the last block
     ours:     size = (i == n_blocks - 1 ? in_size - in_offset : block_size)
     upstream: size = block_size; if (i == n_blocks - 1) size = in_size % block_size;
   The upstream form yields 0 whenever in_size is an exact multiple of
   block_size. karyozip drives bzip3 at 8 to 256 MB block sizes, so an
   aligned payload is reachable. Reproduced with lastblock_check.c:
   133120 bytes at the 65 KiB minimum block size gives, on stock 1.5.3,
   out=1133 and 66560 bytes back, with rc=0 from both calls. Half the
   input, silently. With this fix all 133120 come back and match.

2. bz3_decompress, the per-block size check
     ours:     if (size < 0 || size > (s32)bz3_bound(block_size)) ...
     upstream: if (size < 0 || size > block_size) ...
   A block that compresses larger than its raw size is legal and fits
   bz3_bound; the upstream bound rejects it, so the decoder can refuse a
   block the encoder just wrote.

A third fix this tree used to carry, block_size = bz3_bound(in_size)
rather than in_size + 16, upstream adopted in 1.5.3.

Checked 2026-09-04 against 1.5.3, the current release. Re-check on the
next one with lastblock_check.c; if upstream takes these two, resync and
delete this note. Neither is reported upstream yet.

  gcc -O2 -DVERSION='"x"' -Ibzip3 -o lbc bzip3/lastblock_check.c \
      bzip3/libbz3.c -lpthread && ./lbc
